.TH MEERCATA 1 "2026-10-09" "Meercata v2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
meercata \- transactional CLI-only control plane for Suricata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B meercata
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Meercata provides read-only health reporting, transaction inspection, and a
gated RuleOps development pipeline for Suricata. It has no GUI, web server,
remote API, or generic command execution interface.
.PP
With no command and interactive input/output terminals, Meercata opens its
numbered terminal menu. The menu remains available without configuration and
delegates to existing commands. Writes and delivery require confirmation.
Unmigrated or gated actions are labelled unavailable; the health-event view is
not the v1 threat-alert evidence viewer. No-argument noninteractive invocation
prints help and returns 2. NO_COLOR disables banner color.
.PP
Production rule promotion and IDS/IPS lifecycle operations remain disabled
until their documented qualification gates are complete.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B menu
Open the interactive terminal menu. Requires terminal input and output.
Use 0 or Enter to go back or quit. Health watch is stopped with Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B health
Collect one health report. Use
.B --json
for the versioned machine-readable form or
.B --watch
for repeated collection.
.TP
.B monitor
Record and inspect durable health transitions, verify scheduled freshness,
deliver due transition envelopes, and inspect bounded delivery/dead-letter
state. The delivery-health subcommand reports backlog, age, retries, and
failed-delivery pressure. Delivery destinations and credentials are never accepted as CLI
arguments.
.TP
.B paths
Show fixed production paths.
.TP
.B transactions
List or inspect durable transaction and recovery state.
.TP
.B rules
Inspect, stage, diff, validate, or regress a RuleOps candidate. Promotion is
gated pending production qualification.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/meercata/meercata.toml
Root-owned active configuration. The package installs an example only and
never creates or overwrites this file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/meercata
Controller state, transactions, candidates, privileged recovery receipts, and
the bounded monitor delivery outbox/dead letters.
.TP
.I /var/log/meercata
Controller and privileged audit records.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Health and monitor delivery-health return 0 for healthy, 1 for degraded, 2 for critical, and 3 for an
unknown or configuration error. Monitor freshness returns 0 fresh, 2 stale,
and 3 unknown/uninitialized. Delivery returns 2 when an envelope enters the
dead-letter set. Other commands document their machine output and failure
status in the installed operating contracts.
.SH SECURITY
Privileged operations are restricted to fixed helper operation identifiers.
The CLI accepts no arbitrary executable, shell command, service name, socket
command, or destination path for privileged execution.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
See the operating contracts under
.IR /usr/share/doc/meercata/ .
.SH AUTHORS
Meercata maintainers.
